(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Rationale: Structured dietary interventions addressing meal timing may influence appetite) Tj
T*
(signaling and cardiometabolic risk factors. This study compares the effects of time-) Tj
T*
(restricted versus conventional eating patterns on metabolic and behavioral measures.) Tj
T*
(Methods: A 12-week randomized feeding trial will enroll 40 overweight/obese adults aged) Tj
T*
(50-70 with prediabetes or treated type 2 diabetes. One group will follow a 10-hour eating) Tj
T*
(window; the control group will eat during a standard 16-hour window. Both groups receive) Tj
T*
(nutritionally equivalent calories. Assessments will include three-factor eating behavior) Tj
T*
(questionnaire responses, fasting hormonal markers \(leptin, adiponectin\), inflammatory) Tj
T*
(markers \(C-reactive protein\), and cortisol. Oral glucose tolerance testing and ghrelin) Tj
T*
(measurement will be performed. Statistical comparisons will use non-parametric tests for) Tj
T*
(within- and between-group differences. The trial will examine whether meal timing,) Tj
T*
(independent of calorie reduction, influences appetite physiology and eating patterns.) Tj
